  "scope": "Atomic retained single-column LONG UPDATE with TCNI25, original-image reconstruction and V3 recovery; normal headless Desktop action and parameterized UNION/crosstab read workflows.",
  "qualification": "Local complete independent-image, recovery and headless application checks. No native Microsoft Access/Windows execution.",
  "observations": [
    "Native batch accepts one ordinary unindexed LONG group with at least two original requests. All original cells bind before reservations and one merged DATA placement plan; independent source/record/placement reconstruction compares complete AFTER.",
    "Native cases cover shared pages, cross-page references at the 255-slot boundary, forwarded roots, two-record materialization/growth, NULL/no-op values, stale expectations and protected-byte forgeries.",
    "Original TCNI25 retains all selected requests, including noops, source digest and typed NULL/Int32 carriers. Exact decoder and V3 source reconstruction do not retry old families. Actual V1 and V2 qualification refusals are tested separately.",
    "Access uses positive type/cardinality selection, explicit retained recapture and V3 prepare. Unindexed zero/singleton requests retain original TCNI24/17 behavior.",
    "Runtime evaluates complete original-snapshot assignments before native finish. Late-row DivisionByZero returns no plan/journal. Saved receipts distinguish matched and changed counts without schema changes.",
    "Desktop SQL Run tests exercise No/Yes, save, acknowledgment, stale capabilities and guarded reopen for actual two-row updates. No native windows are opened.",
    "Normal UNION/UNION ALL Run verifies duplicate/NULL membership, first-arm names, typed prompts, cancellation, readonly result authority and late-arm error preservation.",
    "Scratch and actual native saved crosstabs Run through typed prompts; static empty headings, included late aggregate failure, cancel/error result retention and tab-owned results are observed via existing state and rendered widgets.",
    "All Cargo commands use --release with workspace-root target/. Selected boundary counts overlap and are not an additive conformance total."
  ],
